<title>NORWAY: Norway oil exports hit new record in November.</title>
<headline>Norway oil exports hit new record in November.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway said on Friday it exported 93 million barrels of oil in November, the highest level ever for a single month.</p>
<p>Government department Statistics Norway said exports of oil and gas amounted to 15.7 billion crowns in the month, with crude accounting for 13.8 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The average oil price in the period was 148 crowns per barrel, down from 152 crowns in October, but 44 percent up from the average crude price in November 1995.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
